logic:
# baseline assessment
if the CRF specification shows the sum is system-derived rather than site-entered:
    deactivate the rule for this study and report NOT_EVALUATED
else:
    derived = sumOfDiameters(assessment, targets, config)
    if reported_sum is present and |reported_sum - derived.sum| > config.sum_tolerance_mm:
        raise finding

for each follow-up assessment:
    if the CRF specification shows the sum is system-derived rather than site-entered:
        deactivate the rule for this study and report NOT_EVALUATED
    else:
        derived = sumOfDiameters(assessment, targets, config)
        if reported_sum is present and |reported_sum - derived.sum| > config.sum_tolerance_mm:
            raise finding

if any target lesion state in (NOT_EVALUABLE, NOT_DONE)
   and reported target_response not in (NE, PD)
   and not partialSumAlreadyExceeds(PD thresholds): raise finding

for consecutive measurements of the same lesion:
    if |delta| >= config.outlier_abs_mm (default 20) and |pct_delta| >= config.outlier_pct (default 50)
       and interval_days <= config.outlier_window_days (default 90): raise finding
    LLM may downgrade to INFO when a comment explains the change (e.g. cavitation, haemorrhage)

if lesion state == ABSENT at visit i and state == PRESENT with value > 0 at visit j > i:
    raise finding (informational when config.reappearance_is_progression is false,
                   escalate when the site also flagged it as a new lesion)

schedule = config.assessment_schedule            # per visit, captured at AC-11 intake
           # { visit_name: { target_day, window_minus_days, window_plus_days } }

for each assessment a:
    if schedule defines a.visit_name:
        planned = schedule[a.visit_name]
        actual  = days(a.assessment_date - reference_date)
        if actual < planned.target_day - planned.window_minus_days
           or actual > planned.target_day + planned.window_plus_days:
               raise finding
    else:                                         # fallback, uniform schedule
        for consecutive assessments:
            if |interval - config.assessment_interval_days| > config.assessment_window_days:
                raise finding

guards:
  - suppress where the visit is unscheduled or an early-termination assessment
  - suppress where the subject had progressed or discontinued before the expected date

for each assessment with both INVESTIGATOR and BICR responses:
    if responses differ, or progression dates differ by > config.bicr_date_tolerance_days:
        raise finding (INFO by default when the difference does not cross a PD boundary)

for each iUPD timepoint:
    next = next assessment for this subject
    if next is None and subject still on treatment: raise finding (missing confirmation)
    elif next exists and interval not in [config.irecist_confirmation_window_days_min,
                                          config.irecist_confirmation_window_days_max]: raise finding

if a timepoint follows an iUPD, confirmation criteria are NOT met,
   and reported_irecist not in (iCR, iPR, iSD, iUPD, iNE): raise finding
also verify the reset response was derived against the ORIGINAL nadir, not against the iUPD sum

if PD recorded (RECIST 1.1 study, not iRECIST)
   and dosing continued > config.post_pd_treatment_days (default 42) after the PD date
   and no treatment-beyond-progression documentation exists: raise finding

if a query matching this finding has status ANSWERED or CLOSED
   and the finding still evaluates as true against the current data:
       assessment = P-ASSESS-ANSWER(query_text, answer_text, current field values)
       if assessment.classification == JUSTIFIES_CURRENT_DATA and confidence >= 0.70:
           if severity in (CRITICAL, MAJOR):
               surface, flagged 'possibly justified', with the answer quoted
           else:
               suppress permanently as JUSTIFIED_BY_ANSWER; record the justification
       elif assessment.classification == CORRECTION_PROMISED_NOT_MADE:
           surface at original severity, noting the outstanding correction
       else:
           escalate severity by one level (capped at CRITICAL) and surface
